/-!
# Native scalar descent of actual smooth Fourier families

An original jointly smooth unit-torus family defines a genuine globally
smooth scalar on the original period-family total space. Real smoothness
is proved in its unchanged complex quotient atlas through actual local
inverse branches of the original covering map. The resulting global
smooth section has the literal inverse-period pullback on that cover.

This package does not assume or assert descent of differential forms,
a primitive equation, or any cohomological generation statement.
-/
